7]. With the 600-unit inter-hop constraint, forward temporal exploration from 1010 reaches only 2 nodes and never 883 (step_01), and no time-respecting path is enumerable (step_08). Crucially, this is not merely a delta-threshold artefact: even with unlimited waiting, 1010's temporal forward cone spans 264 nodes yet still excludes 883 (step_02), so the failure is structural/directional rather than a matter of timing tightness. Controls: the window is richly active overall (6482 events, 1922 active nodes, step_03), so the negative is not caused by an empty window; but the specific endpoints are sparse \u2014 1010 has only 2 events with a single outgoing partner, 66 (step_04, step_12), while 883 is only ever a receiver from 729, 1038 and 1209 (step_05, step_13). Probing the one viable first hop, node 66, also fails to reach 883 under the 600-unit rule (step_15). Timing further disfavours a cascade: 1010's two events fall in bins ending 60916 and 70516 (step_09), 883's inbound events cluster at 60917-65716 and 70517-75316 (step_10), and 883's in-neighbours are active in overlapping bins (step_14) \u2014 i.e., there is co-active volume near 883 that could superficially suggest influence, but none of it is downstream of 1010. The observable association is background popularity/co-activity, not a genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_78b94701\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883],\n  \"window\": [51317, 89717],\n  \"confidence\": 0.92,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade from 1010 to 883 exists in [51317, 89717]. With the 600-unit inter-hop constraint, forward temporal exploration from 1010 reaches only 2 nodes and never 883 (step_01), and no time-respecting path is enumerable (step_08). Crucially, this is not merely a delta-threshold artefact: even with unlimited waiting, 1010's temporal forward cone spans 264 nodes yet still excludes 883 (step_02), so the failure is structural/directional rather than a matter of timing tightness. Controls: the window is richly active overall (6482 events, 1922 active nodes, step_03), so the negative is not caused by an empty window; but the specific endpoints are sparse \u2014 1010 has only 2 events with a single outgoing partner, 66 (step_04, step_12), while 883 is only ever a receiver from 729, 1038 and 1209 (step_05, step_13). Probing the one viable first hop, node 66, also fails to reach 883 under the 600-unit rule (step_15). Timing further disfavours a cascade: 1010's two events fall in bins ending 60916 and 70516 (step_09), 883's inbound events cluster at 60917-65716 and 70517-75316 (step_10), and 883's in-neighbours are active in overlapping bins (step_14) \u2014 i.e., there is co-active volume near 883 that could superficially suggest influence, but none of it is downstream of 1010. The observable association is background popularity/co-activity, not a genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 63903, "total_output_tokens": 3779, "total_tokens": 67682, "total_latency_ms": 54770, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}